# Ingestion bookkeeping: which corpus files are in the index, by content hash. It
# defaults to a path inside server/data/ (the corpus directory), which the Dockerfile
# COPYs wholesale — so without this line, a developer who has run the server locally
# bakes their own machine's "already ingested" record into the image, and every
# container built from it skips ingestion against an empty index. It is runtime state
# belonging to a particular Qdrant volume, never build input.
server/data/.rag_metadata.sqlite*
